# LF everywhere. `text=auto` normalizes any file git detects as text to LF in
# the object store, and `eol=lf` checks it out as LF on every platform, so a
# clone on Windows carries the same bytes as one on Linux regardless of a
# developer's `core.autocrlf`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Content detection keys on a NUL byte in the first 8 KiB, which every file
# below happens to carry today. Declared anyway: a conformance vector or a
# generated bundle that is accidentally NUL-free must still never be
# line-ending converted, and for `.saci` that would rewrite the wire format
# the corpus exists to pin.
*.saci binary
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.klib binary

# The Pages-served Maven repository is byte-exact: every artifact carries
# committed .md5/.sha1/.sha256/.sha512 files beside it, so an end-of-line
# conversion on checkout would invalidate the checksum Gradle verifies.
docs/static/maven/** -text
